### 3\. Formal assertion

OMNIPOTENCE EUPHORIA, VALIDITY DRIFT & AUTHORITY-CAPACITY DISCREPANCY

Institutional authority cannot establish its own validity through the magnitude of its assertion, executive confidence, preferential recognition, or administrative dominance.

Where institutional executives presume authority beyond their lawful jurisdiction, claim scientific or psychological competence without appropriate qualifications, or exercise responsibilities unsupported by statutory authorization, funded capacity, and independent oversight, an authority-capacity discrepancy emerges.

Such discrepancies warrant examination for validity drift, epistemic displacement, procedural circumvention, fiduciary divergence, and potential institutional usurpation.

The governing distinction: Authority claimed is not necessarily authority conferred; capacity asserted is not necessarily capacity possessed; and institutional confidence is not evidence of institutional validity.

